WEBVTT

00:23.250 --> 00:23.960
I see it!

00:23.960 --> 00:24.750
Over there!

00:24.750 --> 00:27.260
Camera! Sound! Everything ready?

00:27.550 --> 00:30.050
My legend starts here!

00:30.050 --> 00:33.640
Here in front of us is Cenancle Island!

00:33.640 --> 00:36.720
With a top-class resort and cutting-edge city,

00:36.720 --> 00:39.690
I couldn't think of a more exciting place to be!

00:40.140 --> 00:43.360
It's no wonder so many corporations and famous brands have been flocking here.

00:43.360 --> 00:46.940
Celebrities throughout the world are registering in storms to build summer villas here,

00:46.940 --> 00:49.240
on what is the most
sought-after island in the world—

00:49.240 --> 00:51.700
My ass! Who wrote this cheeky garbage!?

00:52.740 --> 00:54.530
We're here already?

00:54.530 --> 00:57.160
Clarion better hurry.

01:07.170 --> 01:10.470
No journalist will ever host her own variety show,

01:10.470 --> 01:13.470
let alone become an actress,
with a crummy script like this—

01:20.060 --> 01:23.020
Why did you jump off!? That mic was expensive!

01:23.020 --> 01:25.110
You all right?

01:25.980 --> 01:27.730
Isn't that...

01:30.150 --> 01:32.820
That console is over twenty years old!

01:32.820 --> 01:35.490
And what's up with that gaming skill she's got going on.

01:39.750 --> 01:42.670
<i>Oh, she's an android.</i>

01:43.580 --> 01:44.630
Hey, redhead.

01:44.630 --> 01:48.340
Code Zero. State your model and owner's name.

01:49.710 --> 01:51.840
<i>If she isn't reacting to the code,</i>

01:51.840 --> 01:54.010
<i>she might be a black-market android.</i>

01:54.430 --> 01:56.760
<i>I guess I'll snatch her for myself.</i>

01:57.760 --> 01:59.520
Hey, you. Code Zero.

02:01.640 --> 02:03.810
Oh, hello. Do you mean me?

02:07.270 --> 02:10.440
Sorry about that. People make that mistake all the time.

02:11.030 --> 02:13.030
I'm human!

02:13.030 --> 02:16.620
I-I know I might not look like it, though!

02:16.620 --> 02:18.370
No, no. It's my fault.

02:18.370 --> 02:20.450
Does that mean you happen to be a full-body...

02:20.450 --> 02:22.540
Th-That's right! I am.

02:22.540 --> 02:23.540
Thank goodness.

02:23.870 --> 02:26.500
Some people have a hard time understanding.

02:26.500 --> 02:28.800
I get mistaken for an illegal android occasionally.

02:29.460 --> 02:32.130
Sorry, I know it's confusing.

02:32.130 --> 02:34.800
But I really wanted to wear a swimsuit. It's been so long...

02:34.800 --> 02:36.180
<i>A full-body cyborg!</i>

02:36.180 --> 02:38.050
Intriguing!

02:38.350 --> 02:40.010
That game of yours, I mean!

02:40.010 --> 02:42.060
Monster Bash, on an old DSD!

02:42.060 --> 02:44.560
When that game came out it was the highlight of my youth!

02:44.560 --> 02:49.150
But this game is over twenty years old...

02:49.900 --> 02:50.650
Oh.

02:51.570 --> 02:53.190
I'm double sorry!

02:53.190 --> 02:56.160
No worries. I'm just shocked to see someone playing an old hand-held

02:56.160 --> 02:58.570
rather than a direct-link game in this day and age.

02:58.570 --> 03:01.990
My doctor gave it to me as part of my rehabilitation.

03:01.990 --> 03:02.830
Intriguing.

03:03.250 --> 03:04.750
But never mind that...

03:08.710 --> 03:12.000
You took your time, didn't you? What'd you find?

03:12.000 --> 03:13.550
I picked this up along the way.

03:15.680 --> 03:18.640
Th-Thank you so much...

03:17.640 --> 03:19.300
What about results?

03:19.300 --> 03:20.300
Results?

03:20.720 --> 03:23.100
Why must you always be so vague, Uzal?

03:23.100 --> 03:26.690
I mean, did you find anything <i>constructive</i>?

03:26.690 --> 03:27.810
Nothing.

03:31.770 --> 03:33.360
They're still clean, right?

03:33.360 --> 03:36.400
C-C-Cute!

03:40.030 --> 03:41.450
Is this your daughter!?

03:41.450 --> 03:43.290
Aren't you an amusing one!

03:44.500 --> 03:48.620
We shall soon arrive at Cenancle Island.

03:48.620 --> 03:51.880
All passengers, please prepare to disembark.

03:54.460 --> 03:56.010
We still haven't introduced ourselves.

03:56.010 --> 03:58.130
I'm Uzal Delilah.

03:58.130 --> 04:01.050
I run a small business on Cenancle Island.

04:01.050 --> 04:03.260
It's nice to meet you, Uzal.

04:03.720 --> 04:05.430
I'm Nanakorobi Nene.

04:05.430 --> 04:07.270
I'm moving to this island today.

04:07.730 --> 04:09.480
Nice to meet you, Nene.

04:09.480 --> 04:11.150
Hmm, "Nanakorobi"?

04:13.480 --> 04:15.780
Uzal has designated me as Clarion.

04:15.780 --> 04:18.240
I am her prized pet.

04:18.240 --> 04:20.910
Side note: anyone who touches these ears goes to hell.

04:23.080 --> 04:25.080
I wanna squeeze you! Till you explode!

04:25.080 --> 04:26.120
Permission denied!

04:26.120 --> 04:28.080
Feel free, to your heart's content.

04:28.580 --> 04:29.920
Just let it happen, Clarion.

04:31.040 --> 04:33.170
Clarion!

04:36.550 --> 04:37.170
Huh?

04:37.510 --> 04:41.300
Careful. She's heavier than she looks.

04:41.300 --> 04:43.680
She's the same as you.

04:43.680 --> 04:44.930
The same?

04:45.390 --> 04:49.730
She's another... full-body cyborg?

04:51.900 --> 04:55.610
This is the first time... I've met someone like me!

04:55.610 --> 04:57.940
Amazing! Please be my friend!

04:58.280 --> 05:00.740
Your body is so cute! No fair!

05:00.740 --> 05:02.660
I'm so envious!

05:02.660 --> 05:05.830
Couldn't you have chosen an appearance you like, too?

05:06.370 --> 05:09.790
This appearance is the result of
a simulation of how I <i>would have</i> looked.

05:09.790 --> 05:12.380
My Mom and Dad gave me this face.

05:12.380 --> 05:14.090
Oh, there's nothing wrong with that.

05:14.630 --> 05:17.050
Your parents, huh? I think I...

05:18.800 --> 05:20.090
I'll tell you what, Nene,

05:20.090 --> 05:22.340
you can cling to Clarion as much as you want.

05:22.680 --> 05:23.720
If you insist!

05:23.720 --> 05:25.890
Don't go bucking, Clarion.

05:26.350 --> 05:28.850
Watch the ears!

05:31.690 --> 05:32.520
Squeezie, squeeze.

05:32.520 --> 05:33.980
By the way, Nene.

05:33.980 --> 05:37.860
What are your plans when you arrive? Something you need to do?

05:37.860 --> 05:38.990
Well, um...

05:39.570 --> 05:42.990
I'm here because my aunt will be taking care of me.

05:43.320 --> 05:44.910
Is that so?

05:44.910 --> 05:46.240
<i>Korobase, eh?</i>

05:46.240 --> 05:48.330
I'm hoping to learn about the world

05:48.330 --> 05:50.710
while I try to repay my aunt for her generosity.

05:50.710 --> 05:52.210
Let's change the question.

05:52.790 --> 05:54.750
If you got your hands on a bunch of money,

05:54.750 --> 05:57.380
and you could obtain any one thing you wanted,

05:57.380 --> 05:58.840
what would it be?

05:59.630 --> 06:00.670
Something I want...

06:00.670 --> 06:02.380
Excluding Clarion.

06:03.840 --> 06:07.390
Um... If I can include my dreams, one thing comes to mind.

06:07.390 --> 06:10.140
It's a bit complex, though.

06:10.140 --> 06:14.150
If you wanted to buy it,
you would probably need a lot of money.

06:14.900 --> 06:16.060
What's that?

06:17.020 --> 06:19.150
World peace!

06:22.820 --> 06:26.160
How fascinating! I can't get enough of you!

06:26.490 --> 06:28.330
Go get some sleep, and think of something else.

06:28.330 --> 06:30.160
And set Clarion free.

06:31.200 --> 06:34.290
When I opened my eyes for the first time as a cyborg,

06:34.290 --> 06:37.420
I was relieved that the world still looked beautiful.

06:37.420 --> 06:41.170
And then I happened upon the idea of it...

06:41.170 --> 06:43.550
Sorry, it's a little difficult to put into words.

06:43.550 --> 06:46.970
Don't worry, I think it's
a surprisingly realistic dream.

06:46.970 --> 06:48.180
You've got my vote.

06:48.550 --> 06:50.470
Work hard to make it come true.

06:50.970 --> 06:51.810
I will!

07:01.480 --> 07:03.820
You should have everything you need to find me.

07:03.820 --> 07:06.200
Once you've settled in, be sure to come visit.

07:06.200 --> 07:08.320
And I'll get to see Clarion again!

07:08.320 --> 07:09.330
No doubt.

07:12.620 --> 07:15.410
Sorry to cut this short, Nene,
but something urgent has come up.

07:15.410 --> 07:16.830
I need to get going.

07:16.830 --> 07:17.790
Oh, of course.

07:17.790 --> 07:19.540
Whoops, I nearly forgot.

07:20.670 --> 07:23.090
Welcome to Cenancle Island!

07:25.300 --> 07:26.470
Thank you!

07:26.840 --> 07:28.590
Say hi to Korobase for me.

07:28.590 --> 07:31.470
Yes, ma'am! And see you later, Clarion!

07:32.060 --> 07:33.720
Nanakorobi Nene.

07:33.720 --> 07:36.980
Hard to believe that's an authorized first-generation.

07:37.440 --> 07:40.480
No wonder Korobase is proud of her.

07:40.480 --> 07:44.240
Hold on. How did she know my aunt's name?

07:44.740 --> 07:46.070
Eh, who cares.

07:49.780 --> 07:52.410
Hey, this is Nene. I'm at the harbor.

07:52.950 --> 07:55.710
Don't worry, I know the address.

07:55.710 --> 07:57.750
Yes. I'll be fine, really.

08:00.000 --> 08:03.210
<i>A brand new place. Brand new smells.</i>

08:03.880 --> 08:06.760
<i>The first time I've met someone like me.</i>

08:07.630 --> 08:09.760
I hope we can be friends.

08:13.140 --> 08:15.270
Even the weather's nice!

08:16.060 --> 08:20.350
<i>Dad, Mom, I feel truly welcome for once!</i>

08:20.350 --> 08:21.520
<i>From now on, I...</i>

08:32.830 --> 08:35.290
What? But that way...

08:35.910 --> 08:36.790
Uzal...

08:37.330 --> 08:38.540
Clarion!

08:42.790 --> 08:44.920
<i>Dad, Mom...</i>

08:57.890 --> 08:59.600
I need to get...

09:00.440 --> 09:01.940
to my friends!

09:03.150 --> 09:05.690
Clarion!

09:07.320 --> 09:10.320
Uzal! Clarion!

09:17.240 --> 09:18.250
There they are!

09:19.540 --> 09:20.750
But they're running towards it?

09:21.790 --> 09:24.750
I can go for about an hour without oxygen.

09:24.750 --> 09:28.760
World peace! Hell, yeah!

09:34.260 --> 09:37.010
Hey fools, I'm back.

09:37.010 --> 09:40.100
What the hell's the meaning of this, Sahar Schehera?

09:40.100 --> 09:42.060
You activated BUER, didn't you?

09:42.060 --> 09:43.020
You bet we did.

09:43.600 --> 09:45.270
And it went berserk, didn't it?

09:45.730 --> 09:47.690
You <i>knew</i> it was defective!?

09:47.690 --> 09:49.400
The entire underground facility has collapsed!

09:49.400 --> 09:51.150
The organization is in shambles!

09:51.150 --> 09:53.610
Because you started it up on your own, you moron.

09:53.610 --> 09:54.700
Moron.

09:54.700 --> 09:56.870
That activation key's a dummy.

09:56.870 --> 09:58.910
The real one's on me.

09:58.910 --> 10:02.920
Did you expect me not to notice this little rebellion of yours behind my back?

10:02.920 --> 10:04.290
How could you do this!?

10:04.290 --> 10:06.710
It even damaged the surface!

10:06.710 --> 10:07.460
Demon!

10:07.460 --> 10:08.340
Fiend!

10:08.340 --> 10:10.010
And you made us wear these clothes too!

10:10.010 --> 10:12.930
Isn't this your own fault for betraying me?

10:13.300 --> 10:15.430
Hand over the real activation key!

10:15.850 --> 10:17.890
Settle down, small fries.

10:17.890 --> 10:20.140
Aren't you all trapped down there?

10:20.140 --> 10:22.560
Shouldn't you be <i>begging</i> me to save you?

10:23.440 --> 10:25.560
Can it!

10:26.360 --> 10:27.230
Look at this mess...

10:27.230 --> 10:28.770
Guess I didn't give them enough paid holidays.

10:28.770 --> 10:29.820
You mean a reason to like you.

10:29.820 --> 10:31.360
Shut up.

10:31.360 --> 10:34.410
All right, Clarion. Pandora Device, open.

10:35.240 --> 10:38.450
Owner's consent, confirmed. Acknowledged.

10:38.450 --> 10:44.080
Release skill, Elpis Series.
Anti Material and Close Quarters Combat.

10:45.710 --> 10:49.340
Uzal! Clarin!

10:49.800 --> 10:50.590
Clarin?

11:06.940 --> 11:08.230
Don't shorten it.

11:10.480 --> 11:11.940
Surround her!

11:11.940 --> 11:13.240
Pincer attack!

11:16.950 --> 11:18.740
Amazing...

11:18.740 --> 11:20.530
Is she another one of Sahar's puppets?

11:20.530 --> 11:21.660
Let's crush her.

11:21.660 --> 11:23.540
Loading the rock drill cartridge!

11:28.000 --> 11:29.500
Make Nene's protection top priority!

11:37.380 --> 11:39.140
Clarin!

11:39.140 --> 11:41.180
This way, Nene.

11:41.180 --> 11:43.430
Hey! We're withdrawing, Clario!

11:43.930 --> 11:44.890
Don't shorten it.

11:54.490 --> 11:55.490
The transmission!

11:55.490 --> 11:57.150
A smoke screen, seriously!?

11:59.240 --> 12:01.240
Clarin!

12:01.910 --> 12:04.290
Forgive me, Clarin!

12:04.290 --> 12:05.290
Don't worry about her.

12:05.290 --> 12:08.250
She's just mad that a mere
excavation bot shortened her arm,

12:08.250 --> 12:11.090
or perhaps even madder we're doing the same to her name.

12:11.090 --> 12:14.420
An arm or two's nothing to fuss about.

12:14.420 --> 12:17.840
Just because it's a prosthetic doesn't make it okay!

12:17.840 --> 12:21.220
Well, it was destroyed protecting you,
so I doubt she even minds.

12:22.470 --> 12:25.390
Anyway, Nene. What are you doing here?

12:25.390 --> 12:26.640
Oh, that's right!

12:26.640 --> 12:29.650
We need to get out of here!
Look what's happening to the city!

12:29.650 --> 12:34.150
I'd love to, hun, but they're blocking our escape.

12:34.150 --> 12:36.400
What are those things?

12:36.400 --> 12:38.700
Bad guys! Criminals!

12:40.110 --> 12:42.280
That's what makes this an emergency.

12:42.280 --> 12:44.490
Perhaps you could help me?

12:44.490 --> 12:47.250
Of course! I'll do anything if it'll help!

12:48.500 --> 12:53.130
Nothing much, I need to write a little data to your body's storage, okay?

12:53.130 --> 12:54.840
There's a very complicated reason for this...

12:54.840 --> 12:56.590
Yes, ma'am! Write away!

12:56.590 --> 12:59.590
Be a little warier of others.

12:59.970 --> 13:01.430
My, oh my...

13:01.430 --> 13:02.680
Hey, Clarin.

13:02.680 --> 13:03.680
Don't shorten it.

13:03.680 --> 13:08.560
We're going to give Nanakorobi Nene
temporary authority to use the Pandora Device.

13:10.480 --> 13:12.190
You're kidding...

13:12.190 --> 13:15.360
Yes. That's the look I taught you, but not quite the right words.

13:15.820 --> 13:18.570
What's a Pandora—

13:19.070 --> 13:21.490
Stick those fingers of yours in here.

13:21.860 --> 13:23.490
My heart can't take this!

13:23.490 --> 13:26.240
I-I'm not into this kind of stuff, uh...

13:26.240 --> 13:28.750
All jokes aside, you need to do this.

13:29.410 --> 13:31.250
Guide her hand, Clarion.

13:35.670 --> 13:38.340
You can connect via your F port, correct?

13:38.340 --> 13:41.470
Y-Yes, but hold on!

13:44.090 --> 13:46.140
Pandora Device, open!

13:46.140 --> 13:50.520
Release skill, Elpis Series. Advanced Firearms!

13:53.400 --> 13:57.230
<i>Deep inside me, where I can't reach...</i>

13:58.820 --> 14:01.530
<i>Not far from there...</i>

14:02.650 --> 14:05.320
<i>I feel something coming inside me!</i>

14:21.970 --> 14:22.760
Behead—

14:23.510 --> 14:24.550
Behold!

14:25.010 --> 14:27.760
The scene in front of us is from Vulcan City on Cenancle Island.

14:27.760 --> 14:31.060
The ground around us is rumbling,
and there are explosions everywhere.

14:31.060 --> 14:35.190
This nearly dangerous report is coming to you live by none other than me, Vlind—

14:42.740 --> 14:43.780
Where's Sahar!?

14:43.780 --> 14:44.780
Get us out of here!

14:44.780 --> 14:45.950
I'm working on it!

14:47.660 --> 14:49.200
I found them!

14:51.700 --> 14:52.700
They're coming!

14:52.700 --> 14:53.710
Left!

14:59.340 --> 15:03.090
I won't let you hurt Clarin again! So there!

15:03.090 --> 15:04.010
What do we do?

15:04.010 --> 15:06.680
There's nothing you <i>can</i> do with these shitty things!

15:06.680 --> 15:09.100
I'm rounding up all the security bots I can find.

15:11.180 --> 15:13.980
Thank you for protecting Clarion.

15:13.980 --> 15:16.480
We think you deserve a reward.

15:17.560 --> 15:18.270
Here.

15:18.940 --> 15:19.730
Oh!

15:20.400 --> 15:22.150
Thank you, Clarin!

15:23.240 --> 15:25.860
Use that to protect us.

15:25.860 --> 15:28.740
But I've spent all this time in rehabilitation.

15:28.740 --> 15:31.030
I've never even touched a gun!

15:33.330 --> 15:34.290
Huh?

15:34.290 --> 15:35.370
Well done.

15:36.620 --> 15:42.130
This isn't my usual cyborg OS.

15:42.500 --> 15:48.010
The application we just installed to you is integrating with your current OS.

15:49.930 --> 15:51.640
It's finished starting up.

15:55.640 --> 15:57.690
Whoa, some other things appeared!

15:57.690 --> 15:59.770
I brought all I could find!

15:59.770 --> 16:03.280
Restrain them!

16:19.000 --> 16:20.420
<i>Just as I thought.</i>

16:20.420 --> 16:22.290
<i>She's an adepter.</i>

16:24.840 --> 16:29.720
The "full-body cyborg" is a technology still in development.

16:29.720 --> 16:34.680
After rigorous rehabilitation, cyborgs are eventually able to handle more difficult movements.

16:34.680 --> 16:37.350
But many people have trouble adapting to the prosthetics.

16:37.350 --> 16:41.400
It will most likely be many years before the technology becomes commonplace.

16:41.400 --> 16:45.110
However, there have been reports of extremely rare cases

16:45.110 --> 16:49.240
where people learn to use their
prosthetics the same as, or rather,

16:49.240 --> 16:51.450
even better than a real body.

16:51.450 --> 16:53.330
Reports are scarce, even globally,

16:53.330 --> 16:56.660
but these "adepters" compensate for the limits of their prosthetic technology

16:56.660 --> 16:58.710
with their own innate abilities and talents.

16:59.460 --> 17:03.960
The info is kept under wraps, but it's known that they are mostly teenagers or younger.

17:04.460 --> 17:06.460
To think we'd happen upon one...

17:08.090 --> 17:11.130
It's an application that aids in
skill-based prosthetics control.

17:12.050 --> 17:14.470
That's what we installed on you.

17:14.890 --> 17:15.970
Another magazine.

17:16.270 --> 17:21.560
It's only temporary, but it has given you the shooting skill of a fully trained professional.

17:21.560 --> 17:24.730
It was essentially designed for humanoid robots,

17:24.730 --> 17:26.730
but you handled it just fine.

17:27.940 --> 17:29.650
I can do something like that?

17:29.650 --> 17:31.240
Look out, here comes more!

17:34.320 --> 17:35.740
<i>It's true...</i>

17:36.330 --> 17:39.040
<i>They seem slow to me, just like before.</i>

17:39.040 --> 17:41.250
<i>I know exactly what to do!</i>

17:53.590 --> 17:55.510
Huh? I don't remember anymore...

17:55.890 --> 17:58.520
It's a temporary supplement,
to keep it out of mischievous hands.

17:58.520 --> 18:01.560
What does this do? Whoops!

17:58.850 --> 18:03.400
Development on it has been shelved,
since it violates about a dozen international laws.

18:03.400 --> 18:04.400
Never mind that!

18:04.400 --> 18:05.270
Clarin!

18:05.270 --> 18:06.900
Were you hurt!?

18:07.520 --> 18:08.820
You're all burnt!

18:08.820 --> 18:12.030
Clarion's fine, but what about yourself?

18:12.030 --> 18:13.780
Yes, ma'am! I'm as good as ever!

18:14.700 --> 18:18.290
I forgot! I need to call my aunt!

18:18.910 --> 18:21.290
Oh no, I can't get through.

18:21.660 --> 18:23.330
Don't worry about Korobase.

18:23.330 --> 18:24.250
Huh?

18:24.250 --> 18:25.580
Korobase Takumi, right?

18:25.580 --> 18:29.300
That's right! Uzal, do you know my aunt?

18:29.670 --> 18:32.300
Believe it or not, we're close friends!

18:32.590 --> 18:34.430
Oh, so that's why!

18:34.760 --> 18:37.930
Well, let's get somewhere safe.

19:00.740 --> 19:02.700
Uzal. Nene's awake.

19:05.210 --> 19:06.330
Clarin!

19:07.500 --> 19:09.040
Why am I naked!?

19:09.710 --> 19:12.130
Clarin, you naughty little girl.

19:12.130 --> 19:13.380
Simpleminded girl...

19:13.380 --> 19:17.220
You collapsed all of a sudden, so we brought you here.

19:17.640 --> 19:18.970
I collapsed?

19:18.970 --> 19:20.810
That's weird.

19:21.350 --> 19:23.480
That's never happened before.

19:24.270 --> 19:25.350
Where are we?

19:25.350 --> 19:26.940
My lab.

19:26.940 --> 19:29.480
It's like my old hospital ward.

19:29.480 --> 19:31.730
Are you a doctor, Uzal?

19:31.730 --> 19:32.690
Sort of.

19:32.690 --> 19:34.610
Uzal, we're out of time.

19:35.610 --> 19:39.320
I-I'm fine, so please repair Clarin's arm first!

19:39.320 --> 19:42.580
Of course. Well, I'd love to, but...

19:43.120 --> 19:45.870
Sahar! Get out here!

19:46.210 --> 19:47.710
Sahar?

19:47.710 --> 19:50.130
The bad guys have found us!

19:50.460 --> 19:52.500
If you won't open the door...

19:54.800 --> 19:55.880
The wall!

19:55.880 --> 19:57.180
We're in a fix!

19:57.180 --> 20:00.010
Clarion! Pandora Device, open!

20:03.270 --> 20:05.770
You know the procedure by now, right Nene?

20:05.770 --> 20:07.520
Y-Yes!

20:07.520 --> 20:09.940
But are you sure Clarion doesn't mind?

20:09.940 --> 20:11.730
There! Just a little more!

20:11.730 --> 20:12.730
Yeah!

20:13.150 --> 20:13.780
I'm fine.

20:13.780 --> 20:16.150
Do it, Nene! It's for world peace!

20:16.150 --> 20:17.740
All right!

20:17.740 --> 20:18.610
Then...

20:22.950 --> 20:24.540
<i>It's coming into me again...</i>

20:24.950 --> 20:27.540
<i>Huh? This feels different than before...</i>

20:51.190 --> 20:52.730
What's this supposed to be!?

20:52.730 --> 20:55.650
It's a camouflage under development that I thought you could use.

20:55.650 --> 20:56.690
Camouflage?

20:56.690 --> 20:59.240
I integrated it inside of you, in a way.

20:59.240 --> 21:00.450
Integrated?

21:00.450 --> 21:05.080
Isn't it natural to hide your identity when you're up to something top secret?

21:05.080 --> 21:07.200
Top secret!? What's that supposed to mean!?

21:07.200 --> 21:08.750
This is the <i>opposite</i> of camouflage!

21:08.750 --> 21:11.250
I have weapons ready for you over there.

21:11.670 --> 21:13.000
Take your pick, honey!

21:19.550 --> 21:21.220
Clarin, stand back!

21:21.220 --> 21:23.260
I heard you, but I refuse.

21:34.770 --> 21:35.520
Huh?

21:38.070 --> 21:41.700
Save us, Mistress Sahar!

21:41.700 --> 21:43.070
We can't take any more!

21:43.070 --> 21:45.950
BUER won't stop!

21:45.950 --> 21:47.990
It just keeps rampaging!

21:47.990 --> 21:50.410
The stop code won't work either!

21:50.410 --> 21:53.540
It's going to bore straight through the base of the island at this rate.

21:53.540 --> 21:56.840
Forgive us, Mistress Sahar!

21:56.840 --> 21:59.130
Don't call me that name.

21:59.130 --> 22:00.550
All right, fine.

22:00.550 --> 22:03.220
I'll stop it, okay?

22:02.010 --> 22:04.800
You know them? Sahar? BUER?

22:04.800 --> 22:06.300
Nene.

22:06.300 --> 22:09.810
You were saying you'd like to buy world peace.

22:12.640 --> 22:17.520
For starters, would you like to try buying peace for this island?

22:18.110 --> 22:19.030
Huh?

22:41.090 --> 22:44.090
Accessing the device named nature

22:44.090 --> 22:47.100
The circuit of infinite synapses

22:49.470 --> 22:52.850
Exchanging loops causes inevitable encounters

22:53.310 --> 22:54.640
Nice to meet you, Clarin!

22:53.560 --> 23:04.150
{talk}{this is pandoradio, it'll change each week, ignore this segemnt}

22:54.640 --> 22:55.850
I hope we'll work well together!

22:55.850 --> 22:58.440
I never authorized that form of address.

22:58.440 --> 23:01.190
Come on, it's so nice and cute.

23:01.190 --> 23:02.150
Clarin.

23:02.150 --> 23:03.610
Disconnect me.

23:04.150 --> 23:05.530
Saving data

23:05.530 --> 23:06.910
Strengthening predictions

23:06.910 --> 23:09.910
Even my latest updates

23:09.910 --> 23:15.210
can't help explain why you're so nice to me

23:15.210 --> 23:16.790
error error

23:16.790 --> 23:18.290
parameter

23:18.290 --> 23:21.630
Please help me understand

23:21.630 --> 23:23.800
where these emotions came from

23:23.800 --> 23:27.010
Find me at the end of this digital maze

23:27.010 --> 23:29.760
of feelings I can no longer control

23:29.760 --> 23:31.770
I understand the concept of emotions

23:31.770 --> 23:35.140
but I can't make any sense of my own

23:35.520 --> 23:38.150
I want to pull out these cords

23:38.480 --> 23:40.900
and head straight to you

23:40.900 --> 23:43.320
I won't come to understand love

23:43.320 --> 23:47.070
without having you here with me

23:53.240 --> 23:54.700
Clarin! Clarin!

23:54.700 --> 23:58.000
What's that big black ball that's underground?

23:58.000 --> 23:59.420
A boring machine.

23:59.420 --> 24:02.880
I wonder if I could get a ball that big rolling.

24:02.880 --> 24:04.550
Boring, not bowling.
